WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:09.150
So I believe that we are getting closer to
the beginning of the middle of the natural

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:15.320
end of Donald Trump's continued, unhinged,
baseless efforts to overturn the results of

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.760
the twenty twenty presidential election.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.070
Donald Trump and others have continued to
insist this is going to the Supreme Court.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.740
The Supreme Court is going to decide and the
Supreme Court is going to do all sorts of

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.300
great things for Donald Trump.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.230
And he will win and he will get another term.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:37.789
Well, the Supreme Court has finally weighed
in for the first time, and they have refused

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:41.570
to block Pennsylvania from formalizing the
victory of Joe Biden.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:47.329
Now, as I'm sure you've heard by now, even
without Pennsylvania, if through some completely

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:52.469
unimaginable circumstance, Pennsylvania went
to Trump, which it's not going to even without

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:54.149
Pennsylvania, Joe Biden would still win.

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:56.949
Joe Biden has three hundred and six electoral
votes.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.870
Pennsylvania is worth twenty.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:03.109
If you take those away from Joe Biden, he
still wins with two hundred and eighty six

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:04.129
electoral votes.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.430
That's six more than the 270 that are required.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:14.750
But the point here is, with five days left
until the official electoral vote is cast

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:20.430
on December 14th, the Supreme Court shows
absolutely no interest and no willingness

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.250
to get involved in holding this up in any
way.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:30.270
This was sort of, well, one of the last ditch
efforts so that you understand the argument

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.270
that was used.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:36.560
Republican Congressman Mike Kelly filed a
lawsuit claiming that when Pennsylvania expanded

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.070
mail in voting in twenty nineteen, it was
illegal under state law.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.520
That was the legal complaint that sort of
worked its way through the system since the

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.520
election.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.250
The court very briefly wrote a rejection notice.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.350
They were asked to throw out the absentee
ballots.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.930
They said, we're not going to do that.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:53.930
They just said no.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:57.690
There were no noted dissents from a single
justice on the court.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.510
Notice also that the arguments they've been
making about why.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:06.960
This election was unfair range dramatically
in some states, the problem is they counted

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.929
the same ballots many times they alleged these
are all unproven allegations.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:14.340
Some states, same ballots counted many, many
times.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.530
Other states, Republican observers weren't
allowed to observe other states expanding

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.600
vote by mail was illegal.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:28.140
Other states sending supposedly unsolicited
ballots was fraudulent in some way.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:34.460
Other states, someone hid and then pulled
out duffel bags of ballots from the ceiling

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.450
or from under a table or wherever they came
from.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:42.930
In some states, dead people voted in, others
people voted twice, etc., etc.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.430
And every single one of these claims in court
have not stood up.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:52.910
And it actually that it's not even accurate
to say that in court they very often don't

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.319
even make these claims.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:03:00.550
It's really common that you'll see a Trump
lawyer on TV say one thing happened when they

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.910
filed the legal complaint to the court.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.810
They don't make the same argument often because
they know there's no evidence of it.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:12.120
Yesterday, also, a Michigan federal court
denied a Republican attempt to preserve election

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.020
data and machines for some kind of future
inspection.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:20.760
So we are having a situation in which these
lame attempts to overturn the election results,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.340
they're kind of naturally winding down Donald
Trump's two primary lawyers on this, Rudy

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:28.400
Giuliani and Janet Ellis, they both now have
coronavirus.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.760
We'll talk about Janet Ellis's diagnosis a
little bit later.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:37.080
Rudy supposedly is going to be appearing at
some events remotely from his hospital room.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.800
But Trump has now lost more than 50 legal
challenges.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:46.300
We're five days from the formal electoral
vote and Donald Trump reportedly might be

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.560
heading to Florida for vacation soon.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.599
There are suspicions he won't even return
to the White House so slowly but surely without

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:57.740
anybody at any point saying it's over.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:58.740
People on Trump's side.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:04.380
I mean, we've been we've called this a month
ago and so did media outlets and states have

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.380
certified.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:10.710
But slowly but surely, this entire thing is
going to kind of evaporate.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:17.720
And on the basis of California now certifying
their election, Biden has formally won more

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.310
than 270 electoral votes.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:27.190
The very final step is for that electoral
vote to actually take place on December 14th,

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:33.240
where the electors designated by each state
say we cast our electoral votes for Joe Biden

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.900
or for Donald Trump, depending on the state
that that they are in.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.210
So we're five days from that.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.900
And I think it will be over at that point,
although, who knows, maybe some will keep

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.930
insisting that Joe Biden won't be sworn in
on January 20th.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.100
He will.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.290
That's it.

